+{
+  "file": "src/flows.ts",
+  "snippet": "returnToolRequests: true,",
+  "cause": "The orderStatus flow passes returnToolRequests: true to ai.generate, so Genkit returns the model's lookupOrder tool request unexecuted and the flow returns the empty text from that turn instead of the final answer.",
+  "evidence": "Genkit's generate option is documented as 'return tool calls for manual processing instead of automatically resolving them' (node_modules/@genkit-ai/ai/lib/prompt-D1LVIkB_.d.mts), and orderStatus never handles tool requests, so it returns an empty text string. The order A-1001 exists in src/orders.json with status shipped, eta 2026-10-22 and tracking NW-7F3K2Q, so the lookup would succeed once the tool runs. Removing the option lets Genkit run lookupOrder and return the model's final reply; npx tsc --noEmit passes. I did not run the flow against the live model."
+}
